"Conan Deploy - Linux":
  stage: Deploy
  image: ubuntu:latest
<% if ci_wheel_only %>
<# No `parallel: matrix` any more. It existed to give each ABI's export tarball
   a leg to restore, back when the ABI fan-out was the only thing that produced
   more than one. Now every taggable configuration exports, and they are not
   all ABIs -- a library build has none -- so the legs no longer line up with
   the tarballs. One job restores the whole set and uploads once, which is also
   one fewer way for two legs to race on the same Conan reference. #>
<# Guarded for the same reason as `artifacts: paths:` above: an empty list
   leaves the key with nothing under it, GitLab parses that as null, and the
   whole file is rejected. Reachable without a deploy misconfiguration --
   `_mark_export_jobs` marks only the jobs whose tag_policy is not "except",
   and a [filter] narrowing the matrix to testing configurations makes every
   Linux job branch-only, while this job stays gated on [ci].deploy alone.
   Dropping the key beats emitting an empty one: with no `dependencies:` GitLab
   hands the job every earlier stage's artifacts, which is the behavior this
   block narrows rather than one it depends on. #>
<% if ci_linux_export_jobs %>
